{"ABACUS", "count_step", R"RASGO(How much the counter adds (or subtracts, if negative) at each CLOCK.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "in:a", R"RASGO(Input A — with no cable, the source is the counter's own ramp (the ABACUS plays melody and rhythm on its own).)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "in:b", R"RASGO(Input B — used in add/subtract/multiply and in the bitwise operations.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "in:clock", R"RASGO(Advances the counter on the rising edge — if free, it uses RATE.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Zeroes the counter and the internal phase.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "modulus", R"RASGO(Modulus of the binary counter — it restarts every MOD ticks of CLOCK.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "op", R"RASGO(Operation between A and B: 0 add, 1 subtract, 2 multiply, 3 remainder (mod RANGE), 4-7 bitwise (AND/OR/XOR/NAND).)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "out:carry", R"RASGO(Short pulse whenever the counter crosses a multiple of MOD — the "turnaround" of the rhythm.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "out:math", R"RASGO(A ⊕ B by OP.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "out:p1", R"RASGO(Bit of the counter chosen by PAT — a clean pulse, a divider.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "out:p2", R"RASGO(P1 XOR the next bit — syncopated.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "out:quant", R"RASGO(A quantised into STEPS steps within RANGE.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "out:rect", R"RASGO(A rectified according to RECT.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "pattern", R"RASGO(Chooses which bit of the counter becomes P1 (and the P1/P2 pair).)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "range", R"RASGO(Voltage window (±RNG) used by MATH/QNT/RECT and by the counter's internal ramp (when A is not connected).)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "rate", R"RASGO(Internal clock of the counter, used only if CLK is free.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "rect_mode", R"RASGO(Rectifier mode: positive half-wave, negative half-wave, full wave, or sign (±RANGE/0).)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "slew", R"RASGO(Smooths MATH and QNT — 0 is an instant step.)RASGO"},
{"ABACUS", "steps", R"RASGO(Number of quantisation steps in QNT.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "agogic", R"RASGO(Weight of the AGOGIC accent: when the previous note lasted much longer than average, this one is accented (the module only knows a duration when the note ends).)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "apex", R"RASGO(Weight of the APEX: the highest note of the last 8 is accented — the high point of the phrase.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "cycle", R"RASGO(The size of the metric cycle, in notes (2–16).)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "depth", R"RASGO(Depth of the VCA, FC and DEC outputs.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "external", R"RASGO(Weight of the EXTERNAL accent (ACC input): CLOCK, TRIGSEQ, PHRASE and BOUNCE work.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "in:accent", R"RASGO(External accent (0–1, continuous or gate).)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "in:gate", R"RASGO(Each rising edge is a note.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(The note's pitch (1 V/oct), for LEAP and APEX.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Back to the 1st beat; clears the tail and the memory.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "inherit", R"RASGO(Inheritance: part of the accent passes to the next note and halves at each note — a tail, not another accent.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "leap", R"RASGO(Weight of the LEAP: the bigger the interval from the previous note, the more accent (an octave or more = full).)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "metric", R"RASGO(Weight of the METRIC cause: the 1st beat of each CYCLE of notes is strong; the others weigh by hierarchy (in a cycle of 8: the 5th ½, the 3rd and 7th ¼).)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "out:cutoff", R"RASGO(Brightness in V/oct (up to +2 octaves): patch it into the FC of a LADDER or FILTER.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "out:decay", R"RASGO(Articulation in negative V/oct: patch it into an ENVELOPE's TIME — the accent shortens the note, as on the 303.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "out:emphasis", R"RASGO(The note's emphasis (0–1), held until the next one.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "out:gate", R"RASGO(The gate, only on accented notes (emphasis ≥ 0.5): to trigger a second sound on the accents.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "out:level", R"RASGO(The emphasis in steps: 0, weak, medium, strong (0, ⅓, ⅔, 1).)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "out:sweep", R"RASGO(The 303 stacking: each note raises a charge by its emphasis and it leaks slowly — accents in a row climb, a lone one does not. Patch it into FC.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "out:vca", R"RASGO(Gain for a VCA: 1 on the accent, down to 0.6 without (at DEPTH 1).)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "rotate", R"RASGO(Rotation: the strong beat moves one position every so many cycles (0 = still; 1 = every cycle). The metre stays, the phase moves.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "suppress", R"RASGO(Suppression: after a strong accent the next one costs more — keeps everything from being accented.)RASGO"},
{"ACCENT", "synco", R"RASGO(Weight of SYNCOPATION: an external accent landing on a weak beat of the cycle weighs more.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "comb", R"RASGO(Spectral comb: it digs valleys into the spectrum. 0 = flat; 1 = 12 teeth, deep valleys — a coarse formant or a comb-filter effect, without filtering anything.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "drift", R"RASGO(Shimmer — each partial gets a micro-detune and an amplitude breathing from slow sinusoids. 0 = deterministic.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "fine", R"RASGO(Fine tuning in cents (±100).)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "fm_amount", R"RASGO(Depth of the linear FM from the FM input.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "freq", R"RASGO(Base frequency. 1 V/oct through the 1V/O input.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "in:fm", R"RASGO(Audio for linear FM (× FM_AMOUNT).)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(1 V/oct CV.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Weaves a new bundle: all fibres whole, new thresholds.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "in:stretch", R"RASGO(CV added to STRCH.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "in:tension", R"RASGO(CV added to TENS — an envelope or a slow LFO here is pressure that builds up.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "in:tilt", R"RASGO(CV added to TILT.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "odd", R"RASGO(Odd/even balance of the partials. 0 = the full series; +1 = odd only (square, clarinet, bright and hollow); −1 = even only (an octave up, a nasal sound).)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "out:intact", R"RASGO(The fraction of the bundle still whole (1 = no scar; near 0 = only the fundamental).)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "out:out", R"RASGO(The sum of the 64 partials, with a gain follower + tanh so it does not blow up.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "out:tear", R"RASGO(A pulse for each fibre that tears (an avalanche gives one pulse).)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "stretch", R"RASGO(Inharmonicity — it stretches or compresses the partials. 0 = harmonic (ratio k); +1 = stretched (a bell, metal, the piano's treble); −1 = compressed (partials close together, dense beating).)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "tension", R"RASGO(FIBRE: the tension on the bundle of partials. Each partial carries load in proportion to how loud it is; past its threshold it TEARS — crackles and falls silent — and its load goes to its neighbours (avalanches). The fundamental never tears. 0 = the usual ADDITIVE.)RASGO"},
{"ADDITIVE", "tilt", R"RASGO(Brightness — the tilt of the spectrum. 0 = dark (the harmonics fall off fast, ~k^-2.6); 1 = almost flat (all 64 partials strong).)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "chance", R"RASGO(Quotations on their own: 0 = only by trigger; 1 = one every ~10 s on average.)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "depth", R"RASGO(How much the present ducks under the quotation (CORRODED, PARENTHESIS).)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "in:in", R"RASGO(The audio APOCRIFO listens to and remembers (the memory keeps the input, never its own output).)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "in:trigger", R"RASGO(Quote now (if there is enough past already).)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "length", R"RASGO(How long the quotation lasts (0.1–3 s). In PARENTHESIS the stuttered passage is ¼ of this.)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "min_age", R"RASGO(How far back, at least, the quotation comes from (5–55 s; up to 60 s of memory).)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "mode", R"RASGO(0 CORRODED: the past comes back reversed and eaten away, the present ducks. 1 CUT: the past comes back clean, splices at zero (a montage cut). 2 PARENTHESIS: the now stutters while the patch goes on.)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "out:active", R"RASGO(High while a quotation plays.)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "out:age", R"RASGO(How far back the last quotation came from (age/60 s).)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "out:out", R"RASGO(The audio, with the quotations.)RASGO"},
{"APOCRIFO", "seed", R"RASGO(Seed: where the quotations come from and when they land (with CHANCE).)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "chord", R"RASGO(The chord to arpeggiate — CHORD's 10 shapes: unison, octaves, fifth, major, minor, sus4, maj7, min7, dim, add9. The CHD CV adds.)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "gate_len", R"RASGO(Length of each note, as a fraction of the step (5–95 %).)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "in:chord_cv", R"RASGO(CV added to CHORD: every 1/9 changes shape.)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "in:clock", R"RASGO(External clock: one note per pulse. Free → the internal clock (RATE).)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Goes back to the start of the cycle on the next step.)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "in:root", R"RASGO(The root in 1 V/oct. It takes HARMONY's ROOT output directly: the arpeggio follows the progression (Rasgo deviation).)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "inversion", R"RASGO(Inversion (0–3): the lowest notes go up an octave — the same chord with another note at the bottom.)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "mode", R"RASGO(The path through the notes: 0 up, 1 down, 2 up-down, 3 up-down repeating the ends, 4 random, 5 shuffle (each cycle a permutation), 6 diverge (from the centre outwards), 7 converge (from the outside in).)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "octaves", R"RASGO(How many octaves the arpeggio spans (1–4).)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "out:eos", R"RASGO(A pulse at the start of each arpeggio cycle.)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "out:gate", R"RASGO(Each note's gate (nothing on steps skipped by SKIP). Patch it into an ENVELOPE or a voice's TRIG.)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "out:pitch", R"RASGO(The current note in 1 V/oct. Patch it into the PITCH of an OSC, WAVETABLE, STRING…)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "rate", R"RASGO(Speed of the internal clock (0.01–40 Hz), used when CLK is free — the ARP plays on load.)RASGO"},
{"ARP", "skip", R"RASGO(Rasgo deviation: chance of a rest on each step (0–1) — the arpeggio breathes. Seeded: deterministic.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "in:in", R"RASGO(Each trigger is a signal (a CLOCK, an ARP, a note).)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Forgiveness: trust goes back to neutral and the refusal ends.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "memory", R"RASGO(How fast trust moves at each resolution (moving average): high = forgets quickly.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "out:betrayal", R"RASGO(A pulse at the moment of betrayal (only after trust had passed 0.65).)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "out:confirm", R"RASGO(The confirmation: a pulse when the window closes and the signal was true.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "out:response", R"RASGO(The response: a pulse at each resolution whose height = trust. After the betrayal it goes silent — the voice refuses.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "out:signal", R"RASGO(The signal — always the same pulse, truth or bluff: nobody can tell by the sound.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "out:trust", R"RASGO(Trust (0–1): rises with truths, falls with bluffs.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "out:truth", R"RASGO(The hidden truth, at the moment of the signal — for whoever wants to cheat.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "seed", R"RASGO(Seed of the game: the same seed, the same truths and lies.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "threshold", R"RASGO(Where trust has to fall, once it was built, to count as betrayal.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "truthfulness", R"RASGO(The truth rate: the chance that each signal is true (confirmed after the window) rather than a bluff.)RASGO"},
{"BLEFE", "window", R"RASGO(The expectation window: how long after the signal the truth is confirmed (0.05–4 s).)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "auto", R"RASGO(On: when the balls stop, they are dropped again — BOUNCE plays by itself forever.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "balls", R"RASGO(How many balls bounce (1–3), each dropped from its own height.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "elastic", R"RASGO(How much the ball gives back at each bounce (0.3–0.95). Each interval shrinks by this factor: the ball's natural accelerando.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "gravity", R"RASGO(Gravity, in heights per s² (1–40): more gravity, faster bounces. 9.8 → the first fall lasts ~0.45 s.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "in:drop", R"RASGO(Drops the balls again at once.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "in:grav_cv", R"RASGO(CV on gravity: each +0.5 doubles the gravity.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "out:accent", R"RASGO(The strength of the last bounce (0–1), held until the next: the accent that falls with the ball.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "out:gate", R"RASGO(A pulse at every bounce of any ball.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "out:h1", R"RASGO(The height of ball 1 (0–1), as a continuous CV.)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "out:h2", R"RASGO(The height of ball 2 (0–1).)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "out:h3", R"RASGO(The height of ball 3 (0–1).)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "spread", R"RASGO(How far apart the drop heights are: 0 = all together; 1 = very different (the balls do not bounce together).)RASGO"},
{"BOUNCE", "wind", R"RASGO(Rasgo deviation: at each bounce, the restitution varies by seeded chance — the rhythm is never that of ideal physics.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "aperture", R"RASGO(Width of the window, a fraction of the period. →0 = a point sample (it becomes a fixed-phase S&H); wide = the average blurs an arc of the wave.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "average", R"RASGO(Depth N of the average: how many captures stack up on the same phase point. A high N = uncorrelated noise disappears (~1/√N), the coherent signal stays.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "blend", R"RASGO(IN ↔ result. 0 = the dry passes through (bypass); 1 = only the processed.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "delay", R"RASGO(Where the sampling window opens, as a fraction of the period measured by TRIG. It turns a "read head" around inside the captured waveform.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "geiger", R"RASGO(Density of a free POISSON gate train on the GEIG output — not tied to any clock. 0 = the output is mute.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "in:in", R"RASGO(Signal to analyse (audio or CV). Disconnected, the module uses an internal noise floor of −34 dB so it has something to reconstruct (it sounds on load).)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "in:sweep", R"RASGO(CV added to DELAY — sweeps the position of the window across the wave (a phrase of positions coming from a SEQUENCE).)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "in:thr", R"RASGO(CV added to the auto-trigger's THRSH threshold.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "in:trig", R"RASGO(Repetition reference — the event the captures lock onto. With no cable: crossings of the threshold (THRSH) or the internal clock (RATE).)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "mode", R"RASGO(0 FOLLOWER — the output holds the average of the last window (a window S&H). 1 RECONSTRUCT — it plays the reconstructed wave in sync with TRIG. 2 OSC — it re-reads the reconstructed buffer at RATE, free of TRIG.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "out:geiger", R"RASGO(Free Poisson gate train (see GEI). A gate of ~5 ms.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "out:out", R"RASGO(The followed / reconstructed signal, mixed with the dry by BLEND. Safety clamp at ±8.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "rate", R"RASGO(Internal clock (if TRIG is free) and re-reading frequency in OSC mode.)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "scan", R"RASGO(Speed and direction with which DELAY sweeps the period on its own. 0 = static (a single point). ≠0 = the window strolls and reconstructs the WHOLE wave (a scanning boxcar).)RASGO"},
{"BOXCAR", "thresh", R"RASGO(Threshold of the auto-trigger: with no cable in TRIG, a rising crossing of IN through this level is the repetition reference (an oscilloscope edge trigger). The THR jack adds CV.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "ceiling", R"RASGO(How many events per cycle, for all voices together (1–32).)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "cycle", R"RASGO(The cycle length with no cable in CLK, in seconds.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "in:clock", R"RASGO(Each pulse opens a new cycle (the budget renews).)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "in:g1", R"RASGO(Voice 1's gates.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "in:g2", R"RASGO(Voice 2's gates.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "in:g3", R"RASGO(Voice 3's gates.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "in:g4", R"RASGO(Voice 4's gates.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "mode", R"RASGO(Off = COMPETE (first come takes it); on = COOPERATE (each voice has its share; the one that spoke a lot yields).)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "out:balance", R"RASGO(What is left of the budget (0–1).)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "out:o1", R"RASGO(Voice 1's gates that fit the budget.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "out:o2", R"RASGO(Voice 2's gates that fit the budget.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "out:o3", R"RASGO(Voice 3's gates that fit the budget.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "out:o4", R"RASGO(Voice 4's gates that fit the budget.)RASGO"},
{"BUDGET", "out:spent", R"RASGO(A pulse when the budget runs out.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "cells", R"RASGO(How many cells the row has (8–24). The row is circular: the last is a neighbour of the first.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "gate_len", R"RASGO(Length of each gate, as a fraction of the step (5–95 %).)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "head", R"RASGO(Where the head reads the row: the cell under it gives the gate; the next three choose the note.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "in:clock", R"RASGO(External clock: one generation per pulse. Free → the internal clock (RATE).)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Draws a new row (seeded) and starts again.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "in:rule_cv", R"RASGO(CV added to the rule: 0–1 sweeps the 256 rules.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "mutate", R"RASGO(Rasgo deviation: chance, at each generation, of flipping one cell (seeded). The rule never fully freezes.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "out:density", R"RASGO(The fraction of live cells (0–1): a CV that follows the life of the row.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "out:eos", R"RASGO(A pulse when the row dies or stops and is reborn by itself.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "out:gate", R"RASGO(Gate when the cell under the head is alive.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "out:pitch", R"RASGO(The note in 1 V/oct: the three cells after the head, read as a binary number, choose a degree of the major pentatonic.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "range", R"RASGO(Extra octaves (0–2): each comes in when the next cell is alive. 0 = only the pentatonic's 8 degrees.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "rate", R"RASGO(Speed of the internal clock (0.05–30 Hz), used when CLK is free — one generation per pulse. CELL plays on load.)RASGO"},
{"CELL", "rule", R"RASGO(The automaton rule (0–255, Wolfram): how each cell is born from its neighbourhood. 30 and 110 are chaotic; 90 draws triangles; 184 moves like traffic.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "damping", R"RASGO(Damping — high settles into a single well; low lets the system oscillate/"hunt" between the two.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "drive", R"RASGO(Strength of the non-linearity — the higher it is, the harder the system is pulled between the two stable wells.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "freeze", R"RASGO(Freezes the dynamics at the current value.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "in:rate_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to RATE.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "in:reseed", R"RASGO(Trigger — repositions x/y at a new random point, without waiting for the system to escape on its own.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "model", R"RASGO(The attractor: WELL (the usual) · RÖSSLER (DRIVE walks the period-doubling route to chaos) · AIZAWA.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "out:out", R"RASGO(The position of the system, always in [−1,1] — the double-well chaotic signal.)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "out:y", R"RASGO(The attractor's second dimension (in WELL, the velocity).)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "out:z", R"RASGO(The attractor's third dimension (in WELL, 0).)RASGO"},
{"CHAOS", "rate", R"RASGO(Speed of the dynamics — from very slow CV (0.02 Hz) to an audio texture (400 Hz).)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "chord", R"RASGO(Chooses the shape of the chord among 10 tables (unison, octaves, fifth, major, minor, sus4, maj7, min7, dim, add9).)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "detune", R"RASGO(Slightly detunes the voices from each other — a chorus.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "drift", R"RASGO(Slow, independent walk per voice.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "freq", R"RASGO(Base frequency — the root of the chord.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "in:chord_cv", R"RASGO(CV that adds to the CHORD knob — modulate it with HARMONY.root for progressions that change on their own.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "in:fm", R"RASGO(Simple linear FM over all the voices.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(1 V/oct CV — adds to the FREQ base.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "inversion", R"RASGO(Raises the lowest voices by one octave — an inversion of the chord.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "out:out", R"RASGO(Normalised sum (1/√voices) of the active voices.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "voices", R"RASGO(How many voices sound (2-4) — fewer voices is a simpler chord even with CHORD high.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "voicing", R"RASGO(Turns on voice leading: on a chord change, each voice slides to the tone CLOSEST to the one it was already playing, instead of jumping straight there.)RASGO"},
{"CHORD", "wave", R"RASGO(Morphs the shape of each voice: saw → pulse → triangle.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "accent_a", R"RASGO(1st accent divisor — ACC triggers when the step is a multiple of ACC-A (and/or of ACC-B, see AND).)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "accent_b", R"RASGO(2nd accent divisor.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "accent_mode", R"RASGO(AND: the accent needs a multiple of A AND of B. Off: a multiple of A OR of B.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "bpm", R"RASGO(Tempo in beats per minute.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "drift", R"RASGO(Slow walk in the effective tempo (±~12%).)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "feel", R"RASGO(Step grouping: straight / triplet / quintuplet / septuplet / nonuplet / 11-tuplet / glitch.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "fill", R"RASGO(How many of the LENGTH steps trigger in EUC.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "gate_len", R"RASGO(Fraction of each step in which CLOCK stays high.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "in:bpm_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to the BPM.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "in:ext_clock", R"RASGO(External clock — when connected, CLOCK follows its rising edges instead of the internal BPM.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "in:rate", R"RASGO(RATE: the tempo multiplied — 1 V doubles, −1 V halves, 0 V is the knob's. Patch TEMPO's RATE here.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Zeroes the position of the euclidean step.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "length", R"RASGO(Number of steps of the euclidean grid (for EUC/ACC).)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "mult", R"RASGO(Multiplier of steps per beat (0.25–8) — how many CLOCK steps fit in one beat.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "out:accent", R"RASGO(Accent — AND/OR of ACC-A and ACC-B.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "out:clock", R"RASGO(Steady step pulse at bpm·mult.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "out:euclid", R"RASGO(Euclidean gate (FILL of LENGTH steps).)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "out:metric", R"RASGO(The metric strength of the step (CV): 1 on the downbeat, ½ in the middle of the cycle, ¼ on the quarters…)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "out:phased", R"RASGO(A second clock slightly faster than CLK: they start together, drift apart and meet again.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "phasing", R"RASGO(How far the PHASE output runs ahead of CLK (0 to 3 %): Steve Reich's phasing. At 0, they move together.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "rotate", R"RASGO(Rotates the euclidean pattern — same density, different phase.)RASGO"},
{"CLOCK", "swing", R"RASGO(Delays the ODD steps within their own slice of time.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "in:gate", R"RASGO(Each gate here is a note. Unpatched, a note is counted when the pitch class changes.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(The line to listen to, in 1 V/oct (only the pitch class counts: 12 notes).)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Forgets the window and clears the pressure.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "out:collapse", R"RASGO(A pulse when the order breaks — to reset a sequencer, kick a pendulum, open a filter.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "out:order", R"RASGO(The order of the line (0–1): 1 = always the same note; 0 = all 12 equally. It is 1 minus the Shannon entropy of the window.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "out:pressure", R"RASGO(The accumulated pressure (0–1): it rises with sustained order and becomes the COLLAPSE pulse when it breaks.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "out:surprise", R"RASGO(How rare the note that just sounded was, in the window before it (0 = the most common, 1 = never heard).)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "patience", R"RASGO(How many predictable notes in a row before it breaks (1–16). Pressure rises 1/PAC per note; an unpredictable note halves it.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "scar", R"RASGO(The scar: for how many notes after a break the pressure does not rise (0–16).)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "threshold", R"RASGO(From what order the line counts as too predictable (0–1). Above it, pressure rises.)RASGO"},
{"COHERENCE", "window", R"RASGO(How many notes COHERENCE remembers to measure the order (4–32).)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "curve1", R"RASGO(Shape of the slew: 0 linear (constant slope — portamento), 1 exponential (RC — an envelope follower).)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "curve2", R"RASGO(The same as CRV1, channel 2.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "drift", R"RASGO(Slow opt-in walk in both offsets — it "humanises" a standing voltage.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "in:in1", R"RASGO(Input of channel 1.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "in:in2", R"RASGO(Input of channel 2.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "offset1", R"RASGO(Constant added after SCALE — with SCALE=0 it becomes a manual voltage source.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "offset2", R"RASGO(The same as OFFSET1, channel 2.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "out:out1", R"RASGO(Processed output of channel 1.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "out:out2", R"RASGO(Processed output of channel 2.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "out:sum", R"RASGO(out1+out2, sum or average according to SUM.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "rectify1", R"RASGO(Continuous rectification: 0 passes, 0.5 half-wave (= exactly max(x,0)), 1 full wave.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "rectify2", R"RASGO(The same as RECT1, channel 2.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "scale1", R"RASGO(Attenuverter of channel 1 — gain from −2 to 2 (negative inverts).)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "scale2", R"RASGO(Attenuverter of channel 2.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "slew1", R"RASGO(Slew time of channel 1 (0-2 s).)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "slew2", R"RASGO(Slew time of channel 2.)RASGO"},
{"CONTROL", "sum_mode", R"RASGO(SUM = the sum (with a ceiling) or the average of the two channels.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "bits", R"RASGO(Quantises the amplitude to 2^bits levels (round(x·L)/L). bits=1 ≈ a square wave; bits=16 ≈ transparent.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "drive", R"RASGO(Gain BEFORE the quantisation — it pushes the signal into overflow (see WRAP).)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "glitch", R"RASGO(Probability, per hold-sample, of a FAULT: a stuck sample (it stays at the previous value), a dropout (silence) or a spike (the previous one amplified). It simulates a bad digital connection / a scratched CD.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "in:in", R"RASGO(Audio to destroy. Disconnected + MIX>0 → the S&H samples its own white noise → a lo-fi/glitch noise source.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "in:mix_mod", R"RASGO(CV added to MIX (the damage comes in by dose, via an ENVELOPE).)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "in:rate_mod", R"RASGO(CV added to RATE.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "jitter", R"RASGO(Instability of the S&H's rate — the clock trembles → pitch instability (the digital 'wow'). Seeded.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "mix", R"RASGO(Dry ↔ destroyed. 0 = straight through (an exact bypass).)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "out:out", R"RASGO(The destroyed signal, mixed with the dry by MIX. Safety clamp at ±4.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "rate", R"RASGO(Rate of the internal sample-and-hold (100 Hz–24 kHz, +CV). Low = a coarse staircase + strong aliasing (the 8-bit 'robot voice') — there is NO anti-alias filter, the aliasing IS the sound.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "tone", R"RASGO(A 1-pole filter on the output (the reconstruction filter, or the lack of it): <0 low-pass (docile), >0 high-pass (only the high-frequency rubbish), 0 neutral.)RASGO"},
{"CRUSH", "wrap", R"RASGO(How the signal that goes past ±1 behaves: 0 CLIPS (it limits), 1 WRAPS (mod(x+1,2)−1 — integer overflow, a brutal sawtooth), between the two a blend.)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "chance", R"RASGO(Gestures on their own: the chance, at each clock pulse, of a random gesture.)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "in:burst", R"RASGO(BURST: slices of the last 8 beats, shuffled like a bag (18–72 ms).)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "in:clock", R"RASGO(The clock: it sets the beat length (without a cable, 120 BPM).)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "in:gap", R"RASGO(GAP: one beat of silence, with 3 ms edges.)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "in:in", R"RASGO(The sound CUT-UP cuts (the last 4 s).)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "in:micro", R"RASGO(MICRO: the start of the last beat, repeated MICRO times.)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "in:stutter", R"RASGO(STUT: the last beat, 4 times (14–160 ms).)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "micro_n", R"RASGO(How many times MICRO repeats the start of the beat (2–8).)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "mix", R"RASGO(How much the gesture replaces the present.)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "out:active", R"RASGO(High while a gesture plays.)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "out:out", R"RASGO(The sound, with the cuts.)RASGO"},
{"CUTUP", "seed", R"RASGO(Seed: the BURST order and the gestures on their own.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "bias", R"RASGO(Probability of the GATE firing at each step (0 never, 1 always).)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "dejavu", R"RASGO(Probability of RE-READING the memory instead of drawing again — the "déjà-vu".)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "in:bias_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to BIAS.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "in:spread_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to SPRD.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "in:trigger", R"RASGO(Advances one step on the rising edge — present, it replaces RATE.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "loop_length", R"RASGO(Size of the circular memory re-read by the déjà-vu.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "out:gate", R"RASGO(Bernoulli gate — fires with probability BIAS at each step.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "out:x", R"RASGO(Drawn CV (or re-read from the déjà-vu), channel X.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "out:y", R"RASGO(Drawn CV (or re-read), channel Y — independent of X.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "rate", R"RASGO(Internal clock, used only if TRIG is free.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "shape", R"RASGO(Shape of the X/Y distribution: 0 uniform, 1 bell-shaped (a sum of 4 uniforms — central limit, no log/cos).)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "slew", R"RASGO(Smooths the transition between drawn values.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "spread", R"RASGO(Span of X/Y — 0 locks close to 0, 1 uses the whole ±1 range.)RASGO"},
{"DECISION", "steps", R"RASGO(Quantises X/Y into STEPS steps — 1 is continuous.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "anchor", R"RASGO(Topology memory — every 8 ticks it records the state as a landmark; with probability ∝ anchor², it returns to the landmark instead of taking a new step.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "bias", R"RASGO(Pushes the field's rest point to one side (it does not stay centred on 0).)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "depth", R"RASGO(Span of the walk — how far the field may move away from rest.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "elastic", R"RASGO(How the field returns to rest: SPRING (the usual) · RUBBER (free in the centre, strong at the edges) · PLASTIC (no return: the rest point moves).)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "in:advance", R"RASGO(Trigger — forces a step (a cadence per bar/phrase instead of the internal RATE).)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "in:capture", R"RASGO(Stores the landmark NOW: the landscape the drift returns to (with ANCHR).)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "in:rate_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to RATE.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "momentum", R"RASGO(How much the speed of the walk tends to carry on instead of reacting on the spot.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "out:a", R"RASGO(Correlated output A — it reads the field with a weight of its own.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "out:b", R"RASGO(Correlated output B — a different weight from A.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "out:c", R"RASGO(Correlated output C.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "out:d", R"RASGO(Correlated output D.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "out:event", R"RASGO(Pulse at every tick of the walk.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "out:field", R"RASGO(The raw shared walk, without the per-output weights.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "rate", R"RASGO(Pace of the shared field's walk — on the scale of MINUTES, not of audio.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "residue", R"RASGO(The return to the landmark is never identical: it shifts the field and flips a bit, by this much.)RASGO"},
{"DRIFT", "stride", R"RASGO(0 = the 4 outputs (A-D) walk almost together; 1 = each goes its own way.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "bend", R"RASGO(Depth of the pitch envelope. 0 = tonal (the frequency stays at TONE); 1 = a kick sweep (it leaps 6× and comes down).)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "decay", R"RASGO(Overall decay time (~20 ms to ~2 s). Short = a click/laser; long = a sustaining sub.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "drift", R"RASGO(Humanisation: each strike varies slightly in pitch/decay/level. From an xorshift seeded and advanced ON the trigger — the same gates → the same audio. 0 = identical strikes.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "drive", R"RASGO(Output saturation (tanh + makeup) — the 909's crunch.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "in:accent", R"RASGO(Accent CV: it scales the level (and the brightness) of the strike. Patch TRIGSEQ.accent here.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "in:gate", R"RASGO(Trigger — one pulse, one strike.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "in:tone", R"RASGO(1 V/oct CV added on top of the TONE knob (tuned toms from a SEQUENCE).)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "map", R"RASGO(Character 808 → 909 → acoustic. As it rises: the body gains a click (tanh), the noise gets higher, a little drive comes in.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "out:out", R"RASGO(The voice — body + crack, saturated by DRIVE.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "roll", R"RASGO(Internal self-triggering. 0 = the external gate only; above that the voice retriggers itself at ~2–40 Hz — a roll, a buzz, and the mode that plays on its own.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "snap", R"RASGO(Dose of the attack noise burst — the snare's 'crack', the hi-hat's hiss, the kick's click.)RASGO"},
{"DRUM", "tone", R"RASGO(Pitch of the body (20–1000 Hz). Low = kick, mid = tom/snare, high = clave. 1 V/oct through the PIT input.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "attack", R"RASGO(How fast it starts turning down once the sound passes the threshold (0.1–200 ms). Fast cuts the hit; slow lets the attack through and compresses the body.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "breath", R"RASGO(Rasgo deviation: the release follows the interval between the hits it hears — the compression breathes with the tempo of the music. 0 = fixed release.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "detect", R"RASGO(RMS on: the detector hears the average energy (~10 ms) — it reacts to the body of the sound, more musical. Off: the peak — it reacts to every hit.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "drift", R"RASGO(Rasgo deviation: at each hit, attack and release vary a little (up to an octave of time) by SEEDED chance — the pumping is never mechanical. 0 = fixed. Deterministic.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "in:in", R"RASGO(The sound to compress (mono or stereo — the channels are detected together). With no cable the module stays silent, like the VCA.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "in:side", R"RASGO(Sidechain: any signal the detector should hear (with SIDE near 1). With no IN and a SIDE, the ENV and GR outputs keep moving — the module becomes a modulation generator.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "in:thr", R"RASGO(CV added to the threshold: −1..+1 = −24..+24 dB.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "knee", R"RASGO(Knee: 0 = compression starts all at once at the threshold; up to 12 dB = it starts gradually before it, more transparent.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "makeup", R"RASGO(Make-up gain after compression (0–24 dB): gives back the level it took.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "mode", R"RASGO(GATE on: it becomes a noise gate (downward expander) — it shuts what stays below the threshold. Off: compressor.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "out:env", R"RASGO(The level the detector hears, as a 0–1 control signal (−60..0 dB), with the same ATK/REL ballistics. An envelope follower.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "out:gr", R"RASGO(How much it is turning down right now, as a 0–1 signal (0..24 dB of reduction). Rasgo deviation: the compression becomes modulation.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "out:out", R"RASGO(The input, compressed (or shut by the gate), with GAIN.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "ratio", R"RASGO(How much it turns down: 4 = every 4 dB above the threshold become 1. At maximum (20) it becomes a limiter: nothing passes the threshold. In GATE, how much it shuts below it.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "release", R"RASGO(How fast it lets go afterwards (5 ms–2 s). Too short makes the sound 'pump'; long holds the reduction between notes.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "side_mix", R"RASGO(What the detector HEARS: 0 = the input itself; 1 = SIDE (any cable). In between, a mix. With no SIDE patched it always hears the input.)RASGO"},
{"DYNAMICS", "thresh", R"RASGO(Threshold: above it (compressor) the sound is turned down; below it (gate) the sound is shut. −48 to 0 dB; the THR CV adds ±24 dB.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "draconic", R"RASGO(The month of nodes (27.21 days on Earth): the Moon's return to where its orbit crosses Earth's plane.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "gate_len", R"RASGO(The gate length (a total eclipse lasts twice as long).)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "in:clock", R"RASGO(Each pulse is one day.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Returns to day 0.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "limit", R"RASGO(The eclipse limit: how far the Moon can be from the node (a fraction of the draconic month; 0.051 is Earth's).)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "out:align", R"RASGO(How close this lunation's new moon is to the node (0–1): it rises as the eclipse season arrives.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "out:moon", R"RASGO(A gate at each lunar eclipse (a full moon near the node).)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "out:new", R"RASGO(A pulse at each new moon.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "out:node", R"RASGO(A pulse each time the Moon passes a node.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "out:phase", R"RASGO(The phase of the Moon (0 = new, 0.5 = full): a month-long LFO.)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "out:sun", R"RASGO(A gate at each solar eclipse (a new moon near the node).)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "speed", R"RASGO(How many days per second (with no cable in CLK).)RASGO"},
{"ECLIPSE", "synodic", R"RASGO(The month of phases (29.53 days on Earth): from new moon to new moon.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "damping", R"RASGO(The loss: little, the chain rings long like a gong; a lot, a short, dry touch.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "in:in", R"RASGO(The sound that makes the chain vibrate (it enters as a force near one end).)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "in:pluck", R"RASGO(A trigger that pulls and releases the chain: the module sounds on its own, like a plucked rubber band.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "in:tune_cv", R"RASGO(V/oct CV on the tuning: the band's tension moves.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "masses", R"RASGO(How many masses the chain has (4–16): more masses, more modes and a denser timbre.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "mix", R"RASGO(The mix between the incoming sound and the chain.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "out:l", R"RASGO(The chain heard at the PICK point.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "out:r", R"RASGO(The chain heard at the mirrored point (the stereo of the material).)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "pickup", R"RASGO(Where the chain is heard: near the end, brighter; in the middle, darker. L and R listen at mirrored points.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "stretch", R"RASGO(Stiffens the spring the more it stretches: with a strong signal, the modes rise and the sound bends.)RASGO"},
{"ELASTIC", "tune", R"RASGO(The spring's tuning (30–1500 Hz): the lowest mode sits below it; the others crowd closer and closer at the top.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "attack", R"RASGO(Rise time — how long it takes to reach the peak after the gate.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "curve", R"RASGO(Shape of the curve — from concave to convex.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "decay", R"RASGO(Fall time after the peak (or down to SUS, if there is one).)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "in:gate", R"RASGO(Gate/trigger that fires the envelope.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "in:in", R"RASGO(Audio input — the ENVELOPE has a VCA built in: it multiplies the audio by the contour.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "in:time_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to the times (ATK/DEC/REL).)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "loop", R"RASGO(LOOP on: the envelope restarts by itself when it ends — an A·D·R cycle that plays without a gate (a gate resets the phase). SUS does not hold: it becomes the level between DEC and REL.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "mode", R"RASGO(TRIG: toggles ADSR ↔ AD (trigger).)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "out:env", R"RASGO(The contour itself, as CV — patchable to modulate another parameter (e.g. FILTER.cutoff).)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "out:eoc", R"RASGO(A pulse at the end of each envelope (or each cycle, with LOOP): to chain envelopes, count cycles, trigger the next sound.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "out:out", R"RASGO(Audio × the contour (the built-in VCA).)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "release", R"RASGO(Fall time after the gate turns off.)RASGO"},
{"ENVELOPE", "sustain", R"RASGO(Level at which the envelope holds while the gate stays on.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "circles", R"RASGO(How many circles (1–8), each spinning on the rim of the previous one.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "detune", R"RASGO(Detunes the speeds by irrational amounts: with DETUNE > 0 the figure never closes.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(1 V/oct on the speed: to play the figure as a note.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Returns all circles to the start.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "mode", R"RASGO(Speeds and radii: SQUARE (odd, 1/k) · SAW (1, 2, 3…, 1/k) · FIB-RADIUS (radii 1/Fₙ) · FIB-SPEED (speeds Fₙ). Different choices, named.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "out:angle", R"RASGO(The figure's angle (0..1).)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "out:gate", R"RASGO(A pulse each time Y crosses zero going up: the rhythm of the drawing.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "out:radius", R"RASGO(The distance from the centre (0..1): it pulses as the circles add up and cancel.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "out:x", R"RASGO(The figure's X coordinate (−1..1).)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "out:y", R"RASGO(The figure's Y coordinate (−1..1).)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "phase", R"RASGO(The starting phase of all circles.)RASGO"},
{"EPICYCLE", "rate", R"RASGO(The speed of the first circle (0.01 Hz to 2 kHz): slow is gesture and rhythm; at audio rate the figure becomes timbre.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "cutoff", R"RASGO(Cutoff frequency — above it, the sound is attenuated.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "drive", R"RASGO(Input gain — it pushes the signal into gentle saturation.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "in:cutoff_mod", R"RASGO(CV (1 V/oct) that ADDS to the CUT knob.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "in:in", R"RASGO(Audio input to filter.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "in:res_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to RESO.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "in:spread_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to SPRD.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "out:all", R"RASGO(The sum of the 3 outputs — the one most used to leave the filter.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "out:center", R"RASGO(Central resonant output (band-pass).)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "out:high", R"RASGO(Isolated treble output (high-pass).)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "out:low", R"RASGO(Isolated bass output (low-pass).)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "resonance", R"RASGO(Lifts the frequencies near the cutoff.)RASGO"},
{"FILTER", "spread", R"RASGO(Spreads the 3 outputs (low/center/high) across different frequencies.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "depth", R"RASGO(The contrast in dB between valley and climax (3 to 24 dB; 11 is the value measured in Studio). The gain never goes above 0 dB.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "follow1", R"RASGO(How much layer 1 follows the arc: 0 stays constant, 1 follows it all. Layer 1 is the essential one (drops less in the valleys); layer 4 is the ornament (drops more).)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "follow2", R"RASGO(How much layer 2 follows the arc: 0 stays constant, 1 follows it all. Layer 1 is the essential one (drops less in the valleys); layer 4 is the ornament (drops more).)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "follow3", R"RASGO(How much layer 3 follows the arc: 0 stays constant, 1 follows it all. Layer 1 is the essential one (drops less in the valleys); layer 4 is the ornament (drops more).)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "follow4", R"RASGO(How much layer 4 follows the arc: 0 stays constant, 1 follows it all. Layer 1 is the essential one (drops less in the valleys); layer 4 is the ornament (drops more).)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "gesture", R"RASGO(The chance of the gestures: the breath (a short silence just before the climax) and, in KISHŌ, the subito at the turn.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "grammar", R"RASGO(The shape of the piece: 0 ARC (rises to the climax and falls), 1 WAVES, 2 GROWTH (successive rises), 3 LULL (calm between two agitations), 4 KISHŌ (the turn is a hard cut).)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:clock", R"RASGO(Optional: with a clock, section changes land on the beat.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:env", R"RASGO(The energy to follow in FOLLOW mode (0–1), e.g. from LISTEN or DYNAMICS ENV.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:in1", R"RASGO(Layer 1: the sound that comes in and leaves at O1 with the shape's dynamics.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:in2", R"RASGO(Layer 2: the sound that comes in and leaves at O2 with the shape's dynamics.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:in3", R"RASGO(Layer 3: the sound that comes in and leaves at O3 with the shape's dynamics.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:in4", R"RASGO(Layer 4: the sound that comes in and leaves at O4 with the shape's dynamics.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:next", R"RASGO(A pulse here moves to the next section.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "in:reset", R"RASGO(A pulse here starts the piece again.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "length", R"RASGO(The approximate length of the piece, from 1 to 20 minutes. The real length comes from the walk through the sections.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "loop", R"RASGO(On, after the coda the piece starts again (a new piece) in 2 seconds. Off, it ends in silence.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "mode", R"RASGO(Where the tension comes from: 0 IMPOSE (the arc), 1 FOLLOW (the energy at ENV), 2 OPPOSE (the inverted arc).)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:breath", R"RASGO(High during the breath before the climax.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:climax", R"RASGO(A pulse on reaching the climax.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:end", R"RASGO(High when the coda ends — patch it into TEMPO's CODA for the final ritardando.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:mix", R"RASGO(The four layers summed.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:out1", R"RASGO(Layer 1 with the crescendo, diminuendo, breath and morendo.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:out2", R"RASGO(Layer 2 with the crescendo, diminuendo, breath and morendo.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:out3", R"RASGO(Layer 3 with the crescendo, diminuendo, breath and morendo.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:out4", R"RASGO(Layer 4 with the crescendo, diminuendo, breath and morendo.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:role", R"RASGO(The section's role in steps: intro 0, rise ¼, climax ½, fall ¾, coda 1.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:section", R"RASGO(A pulse at each section change.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "out:tension", R"RASGO(The shape's tension, 0–1: patch it into a cutoff, a FILL or TEMPO's TENS so everything follows the shape.)RASGO"},
{"FORM", "seed", R"RASGO(The seed of the walk: the same SEED gives the same shape.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "drift", R"RASGO(Each formant gets a slow, independent wobble (±drift·3 %) — the voice breathes. Deterministic (sines, no RNG). 0 = static.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "in:in", R"RASGO(The CARRIER — what is going to be shaped (a saw OSC, a pad, NOISE). In vocoder mode it is the 'synthetic' voice that speaks.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "in:mod", R"RASGO(The vocoder's MODULATOR — the sound whose spectral envelope will control the 5 bands (a voice, a DRUM, a recording). It only has an effect with VOCODER > 0.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "in:shift", R"RASGO(CV added to SHIFT.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "in:vowel", R"RASGO(CV added to VOWEL (an LFO, a SEQUENCE, an envelope…).)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "mix", R"RASGO(Dry ↔ resonated. 0 = straight through.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "out:out", R"RASGO(Dry + the 5 bands, mixed by MIX, with a gentle limiter.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "res", R"RASGO(Narrows the 5 bands (width ÷ (1 + res·8)). 0 = a subtle colouration; 1 = bands that sing/whistle.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "shift", R"RASGO(Scales ALL the formant frequencies (2^(shift·1.5), ≈ 0.35× to 2.8×) — the length of the vocal tract: down = a big/low voice, up = a small/high voice.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "vocoder", R"RASGO(Blends towards VOCODER mode: the GAINS of the 5 bands start following the energy of the MODULATOR (the MOD jack) at each formant frequency, instead of the vowel table. 0 = classic FORMANT; 1 = a 5-band vocoder.)RASGO"},
{"FORMANT", "vowel", R"RASGO(Position in the vowel sequence A → E → I → O → U. Each vowel is a set of 5 formants (spectral peaks); the knob interpolates between the neighbours.)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "in:gate", R"RASGO(Each note (SCOPE.ONS works); the end of the gate measures the rest.)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(The player's pitch (1 V/oct): SCOPE.PIT works.)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "memory", R"RASGO(Over how many notes the reference (the recent maxima) fades.)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "min_notes", R"RASGO(The minimum length of a cell, in notes.)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "out:boundary", R"RASGO(A pulse when a new cell starts — one note later (to know whether a note is a boundary the next one has to be heard).)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "out:end", R"RASGO(A pulse when silence closes the phrase.)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "out:notes", R"RASGO(The length of the last closed cell (notes/16).)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "out:strength", R"RASGO(The boundary strength of the last note (0–1).)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "silence", R"RASGO(Silence that closes the phrase at once (0.3–4 s): a pulse at END.)RASGO"},
{"FRONTEIRA", "threshold", R"RASGO(The minimum strength for a boundary (0.05–0.9): low = short, many cells.)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "drift", R"RASGO(Slow, correlated walk in the effective rate — time "breathes" with no input at all.)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "in:rate_mod", R"RASGO(1 V/oct CV that multiplies RATE.)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "in:slope_mod", R"RASGO(CV that adds to SLOPE.)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "in:sync", R"RASGO(Hard sync trigger (needs SYNC on).)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "out:bi", R"RASGO(Bipolar output (−1..1) — good for pitch/FM CV.)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "out:uni", R"RASGO(Unipolar output (0..1) — good for an amplitude envelope/LFO.)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "rate", R"RASGO(Speed of the ramp — from an LFO (0.01 Hz) to an audio oscillator (12 kHz).)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "slope", R"RASGO(Shape of the ramp: 0 falling sawtooth, 0.5 triangle, 1 rising sawtooth.)RASGO"},
{"FUNCTION", "sync_enable", R"RASGO(Turns on the response to the SYNC jack (it restarts the phase).)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "amp_step", R"RASGO(The step of the amplitudes' random walk: 0, a still shape; high, the wave stirs.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "band", R"RASGO(How far the pitch may wander: 0, a tuned note that breathes; 1, the period wanders freely, up to noise.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "dist", R"RASGO(The distribution of the steps: 0 uniform, 1 Gaussian, 2 Cauchy (rare, large jumps, Xenakis's favourite), 3 logistic.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "dur_step", R"RASGO(The step of the durations' random walk between the points.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "freq", R"RASGO(The central pitch (20–2000 Hz).)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "in:amp_cv", R"RASGO(CV added to the amplitudes' step.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "in:freeze", R"RASGO(With the gate high, the walk stops and the wave repeats: the frozen portrait of an instant.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(The pitch in V/oct, added to FREQ.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "level", R"RASGO(The output level.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "out:out", R"RASGO(The sound.)RASGO"},
{"GENDYN", "points", R"RASGO(How many points the wave's polygon has (3–16): few, a clearer buzz; many, a grainier sound.)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "curve", R"RASGO(Shape of the glide: 0 = linear (constant speed, it arrives at the exact time — MS-20/Minimoog); 1 = exponential (RC, it drags at the arrival).)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "fall", R"RASGO(Asymmetry: fall time = TIME·6^FALL. −1 = a fall 6× faster than the rise; +1 = 6× slower; 0 = symmetric.)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "in:gate", R"RASGO(Note gate, for MODE 2 (legato): a rising edge = a detached attack (it jumps); sustained = it glides.)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(Note CV to lead (1 V/oct or anything). With no cable, the output freezes at the last value.)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "in:slide", R"RASGO(Gate that enables the glide in MODE 1 — bring it from a TRIGSEQ/TURING line for generative slide.)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "mode", R"RASGO(0 = it always glides (classic portamento); 1 = only while SLIDE is high (the TB-303's slide, each step decides); 2 = legato (it glides only if GATE stays high through the change; a new gate jumps).)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "out:done", R"RASGO(A ~2 ms pulse when it reaches the target — for an accent, a ratchet or a timbre change to react to "arrived".)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "out:moving", R"RASGO(High while it is gliding.)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "out:out", R"RASGO(The note CV, now led.)RASGO"},
{"GLIDE", "time", R"RASGO(Time of the glide on the WAY UP — for a change of 1.0 (one octave). 0 = a dry jump.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "damp", R"RASGO(A low-pass inside each line's loop — the treble decays before the bass, as in a real room. 0 = bright, 1 = dark.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "decay", R"RASGO(Tail time (RT60): 0.2 s to 15 s. Close to maximum the tail hardly decays at all.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "in:decay", R"RASGO(CV added to DECAY.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "in:freeze", R"RASGO(Gate: while high, the tail becomes infinite (g = 1, the network preserves energy) and new input stops coming in — like the LOOPER's HOLD, but for the space.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "in:in", R"RASGO(Audio to reverberate (summed to mono).)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "in:size", R"RASGO(CV added to SIZE.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "mix", R"RASGO(Dry ↔ wet. 0 = straight through.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "mod", R"RASGO(Depth of the modulation of each line's read point (slow LFOs, distinct phases) — chorus on the tail, it breaks the metallic 'whistle'. Deterministic, no RNG.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "out:l", R"RASGO(Left channel (a combination of the even lines).)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "out:r", R"RASGO(Right channel (odd lines) — decorrelated from L so the image comes out wide.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "pre", R"RASGO(Pre-delay: 0 to ~120 ms before the network. It separates the direct sound from the reverberation — what defines the perceived size.)RASGO"},
{"HALL", "size", R"RASGO(Size of the space — it scales the 8 line lengths from ~8 ms (a room) to ~88 ms (a hall).)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "hold", R"RASGO(Probability of SKIPPING a scheduled change, keeping the current tonal centre.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "in:advance", R"RASGO(Trigger — moves on to the next tonal centre on the rising edge; present, it replaces RATE.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Back to the initial ROOT/scale.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "movement", R"RASGO(Harmonic movement technique: Coltrane / tritone substitution+ii-V / chromatic mediant / modal interchange / modal jazz / backdoor ii-V / NEO-RIEMANN (P, L, R: each step moves a single note of the triad).)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "nr_cycle", R"RASGO(NEO-RIEMANN only: the path through the triads — 0 free walk (never undoes the step), 1 hexatonic (P L…: closes in 6), 2 octatonic (P R…: closes in 8), 3 LR (the walking fifths).)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "out:change", R"RASGO(Short pulse (~20 ms) every time ROOT or SCALE really change.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "out:op", R"RASGO(Which transformation happened at the last NEO-RIEMANN advance: P = ⅓, L = ⅔, R = 1. For the patch to react to each kind of motion.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "out:root", R"RASGO(New root, as CV (semitone/12) — plug it into the ROOT input of QUANTIZER.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "out:scale", R"RASGO(New scale index, as CV (index/11) — plug it into the SCL input of QUANTIZER.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "rate", R"RASGO(Internal clock, used only if ADV is free.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "root_start", R"RASGO(Root note at reset/start (0=C ... 11=B).)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "scale_hi", R"RASGO(Highest scale index that can be drawn on a change.)RASGO"},
{"HARMONY", "scale_lo", R"RASGO(Lowest scale index that can be drawn on a change.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "coherence", R"RASGO(Coherence: 1, laser light (sharp fringes); 0, lamp light (the phase wanders and the pattern turns to haze).)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "in:ratio_cv", R"RASGO(CV added to RATIO.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Returns the observation point to the centre of the screen (a bright fringe).)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "in:speed_cv", R"RASGO(V/oct CV on the speed.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "out:dark", R"RASGO(A pulse at each dark fringe.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "out:fringe", R"RASGO(A pulse at each bright fringe.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "out:int", R"RASGO(The light intensity at the point (0–1); with a high SPEED, a sound.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "out:moire", R"RASGO(The slow envelope of the fringes (the moiré), 0–1.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "ratio", R"RASGO(The third source's path difference, as a multiple of the first: near 1, the fringes group into a moiré.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "speed", R"RASGO(How many bright fringes per second (0.05–2000): slow, it is rhythm; at audio rate, INT becomes timbre.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "third", R"RASGO(The third source's amplitude: 0, two sources and regular fringes; 1, the strongest moiré.)RASGO"},
{"INTERFERENCE", "threshold", R"RASGO(The bright-fringe threshold (the dark one uses the mirror, 1 − THR): high, only the brightest peaks give a pulse.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "brightness", R"RASGO(BRIGHTNESS axis: adds to BRT.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "drift", R"RASGO(How much the three axes drift on their own, slowly (a mood lasting several phrases).)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "energy", R"RASGO(CHARACTER axis ENERGY: more marcato, wider vibrato, bigger overshoot.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "expression", R"RASGO(How much the interpreter acts (0 = the raw note).)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "glide", R"RASGO(The base glide (longer on leaps and with SOFTNESS).)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "in:character", R"RASGO(CV added to ENERGY.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "in:gate", R"RASGO(The notes' gates.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(The incoming notes (1 V/oct), from any sequencer.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "out:amp", R"RASGO(Articulation (legato, staccato, marcato, tenuto, from context) and breath.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "out:bright", R"RASGO(Brightness: register, apex and the BRIGHTNESS axis.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "out:gate", R"RASGO(The articulated gate (staccato shortens it).)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "out:phrase", R"RASGO(The phrase state: calm 0 · rising ⅓ · climax ⅔ · release 1.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "out:pitch", R"RASGO(The played pitch: glide, overshoot on leaps, progressive vibrato.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "softness", R"RASGO(SOFTNESS axis: long glides, more legato, softer attacks.)RASGO"},
{"INTERPRET", "vibrato", R"RASGO(Vibrato on long notes: it starts after 0.25 s and grows.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "in:gate", R"RASGO(Each gate here is a note (SCOPE.ONS works). Unpatched, a note is counted when the pitch class changes.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "in:pitch", R"RASGO(The line of whoever plays, in 1 V/oct (only the pitch class counts). SIGNAL-IN → SCOPE.PIT works.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Forgets what it heard and goes back to having no key.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "memory", R"RASGO(How long KEY remembers (2–60 s): short follows modulations quickly; long stays firm in the key.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "out:certainty", R"RASGO(How clear the key is (0–1): the margin to the second most likely key. Real ambiguity (relative keys, chromaticism) gives low certainty.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "out:changed", R"RASGO(A pulse when the key changes.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "out:root", R"RASGO(The tonic, in the QUANTIZER format: patch it into ROOT. It is also the tonic in 1 V/oct.)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "out:scale", R"RASGO(Major or minor, in the QUANTIZER format: patch it into SCL (Major or natural minor).)RASGO"},
{"KEY", "stability", R"RASGO(How many notes in a row a new key must win to count (1–16): avoids flickering between neighbouring keys.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "comp", R"RASGO(Bass compensation: when the resonance rises, the ladder loses its bass. At 1 the bass gain returns to 1 at any RESO; at 0 the bass sinks as in the original ladder.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "cutoff", R"RASGO(The cutoff frequency (20 Hz–20 kHz). The resonance peak sits exactly here, at any DIODE.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "diode", R"RASGO(The coupling between the rungs: 0 = transistor (isolated rungs, round); 1 = diode (each rung loads its neighbour, acid); in between, ladders that do not exist as circuits.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "drive", R"RASGO(Pushes the input against the loop's saturation (up to ≈ +18 dB): the sound compresses and fattens; the output level is compensated.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "in:cutoff_mod", R"RASGO(CV on the cutoff, 1 V/oct: an envelope here makes the subtractive bass; a note here tunes the self-oscillation.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "in:in", R"RASGO(The audio to filter.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "in:res_mod", R"RASGO(CV added to RESO.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "out:lp2", R"RASGO(12 dB/oct low-pass (the 2nd-rung tap, with the same feedback): brighter, same resonance.)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "out:lp4", R"RASGO(24 dB/oct low-pass (all four rungs).)RASGO"},
{"LADDER", "resonance", R"RASGO(The ladder's feedback: the peak at the cutoff grows and, near 1, the ladder self-oscillates into a sine tuned to CUT. RESO 1 is the threshold computed for each DIODE.)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "blur", R"RASGO(How much what is out of focus blurs in time (the attack spreads).)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "depth", R"RASGO(The depth of field, in octaves (the aperture): small, only the focus stays sharp; large, almost everything.)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "focus", R"RASGO(The frequency in focus (60–8000 Hz): its band stays sharp.)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "in:blur_cv", R"RASGO(CV added to BLUR.)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "in:focus_cv", R"RASGO(V/oct CV on the focus: the lens hunts.)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "in:in", R"RASGO(The sound that passes through the lens.)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "mix", R"RASGO(How much of the blur comes in (0 = the untouched input).)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "out:l", R"RASGO(The left output: what is out of focus widens in the stereo field.)RASGO"},
{"LENS", "out:r", R"RASGO(The right output.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "delay", R"RASGO(Delay of the DIV pulse (0-200 ms), in a sample ring.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "divide", R"RASGO(Modulo-N counter over the edges of CLK — DIV pulses once every N.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "gate_len", R"RASGO(Duty of the DIV pulse.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "in:a", R"RASGO(Input A of the AND/OR/XOR logic and of the flip-flop.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "in:b", R"RASGO(Input B of the AND/OR/XOR logic.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "in:clock", R"RASGO(External clock — when connected, it replaces the internal clock.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Zeroes the division counter and the flip-flop.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "multiply", R"RASGO(Measures the period between CLK edges and schedules sub-ticks inside it — multiplies the density without needing a faster clock from outside.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "out:and", R"RASGO(A AND B, level by level.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "out:div", R"RASGO(Pulse of the divider/multiplier, with DELAY and GATE applied.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "out:flip", R"RASGO(T-type flip-flop — toggles state on every rising edge of A.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "out:or", R"RASGO(A OR B.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "out:xor", R"RASGO(A XOR B.)RASGO"},
{"LOGIC", "rate", R"RASGO(Internal clock, used only when CLK is free — LOGIC on its own becomes a rhythm generator.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "age", R"RASGO(Tape/BBD character: loss of treble in the loop, wow & flutter, saturation and hiss.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "feedback", R"RASGO(How much of the output comes back into the loop — above 1 it self-oscillates.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "heads", R"RASGO(1 head = a simple echo. 2–4 = a MULTI-HEAD tape echo (Space Echo): the extra heads read fractions of TIME (0.75 / 0.5 / 0.25×) and sum — a dense, rhythmic echo.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "hold", R"RASGO(Freezes the loop: it stops writing and repeats the current window forever.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "in:freeze", R"RASGO(Gate: while high, it is the same as HOLD on.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "in:in", R"RASGO(Audio input.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "in:rev", R"RASGO(Gate: while high, it is the same as REV on.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "in:time", R"RASGO(CV that adds to TIME (in seconds).)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "mix", R"RASGO(Dry ↔ wet on the OUT output.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "out:out", R"RASGO(Dry + wet, mixed by MIX.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "out:wet", R"RASGO(Only the loop, without the dry.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "reverse", R"RASGO(Reads the loop backwards, with no click.)RASGO"},
{"LOOPER", "time", R"RASGO(Length of the delay — from a short echo to a 2 s loop.)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "bounce", R"RASGO(Post-strike overshoot — a damped sinusoid adds to the envelope right after the STRIKE, simulating the vactrol's "bounce".)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "drift", R"RASGO(Slow, correlated walk in the response tail.)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "in:cv", R"RASGO(CV that adds to STRIKE — it opens the LPG from outside, with no trigger.)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "in:in", R"RASGO(Audio input to strike.)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "in:strike", R"RASGO(Trigger — it opens the envelope on the rising edge, the "strike".)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "mode", R"RASGO(Filter↔VCA crossfade — 0 filter only, 1 VCA only, 0.5 both fully active (the classic LPG, it closes completely when the envelope falls to 0).)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "offset", R"RASGO(Resting opening — how far the LPG stays open even with no strike.)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "out:out", R"RASGO(Audio × the vactrol envelope — the plucky west-coast timbre.)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "resonance", R"RASGO(Resonance of the 2-pole filter.)RASGO"},
{"LPG", "response", R"RASGO(Time of the post-strike tail (~30 ms to 2.5 s) — the "memory" of the simulated LDR.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "coupling", R"RASGO(Coupling: positive, each magnet wants to copy its neighbours (ferromagnet); negative, to oppose them (a chessboard).)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "field", R"RASGO(An external magnet pushing the whole grid up or down.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "gate_len", R"RASGO(The gate length, as a fraction of the pulse.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "in:clock", R"RASGO(Each pulse: the grid stirs and the head moves one cell.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "in:field_cv", R"RASGO(CV on the external field.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "in:quench", R"RASGO(Heats everything at once: the grid turns to noise and organises again.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "in:temp_cv", R"RASGO(CV on the temperature.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "out:energy", R"RASGO(Energy per magnet (0 = minimum … 1 = maximum).)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "out:flips", R"RASGO(How much of the grid flipped this pulse (0–1).)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "out:gate", R"RASGO(Gate when the magnet under the head points up.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "out:mag", R"RASGO(Magnetisation (−1..1): where the whole grid points.)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "rate", R"RASGO(The internal clock (with no cable in CLK).)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "sweep", R"RASGO(How many flip attempts per pulse (fraction of the grid).)RASGO"},
{"MAGNET", "temp", R"RASGO(Temperature (0.1–6): low, the magnets align in large domains; high, noise wins; near 2.27 (critical), domains of every size — the edge of chaos.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "gate_len", R"RASGO(Length of each note, as a fraction of the step (5–95 %).)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "in:clock", R"RASGO(External clock: one note per pulse. Free → the internal clock (RATE).)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "in:learn_gate", R"RASGO(Each gate here reads LRN.P and counts a transition from the previous note to this one.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "in:learn_pitch", R"RASGO(The pitch to learn, in 1 V/oct (only the pitch class counts: 12 notes).)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "in:reset", R"RASGO(Forgets everything and goes back to the pentatonic walk.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "learn", R"RASGO(On: learns what arrives at LRN.P/LRN.G. Off: freezes what it learned and only improvises.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "memory", R"RASGO(How much it remembers: 1 = never forgets; near 0 = old transitions fade and the chain follows what is playing now.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "octave", R"RASGO(Transposes the output by octaves (−2..+2).)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "out:gate", R"RASGO(The gate of each improvised note.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "out:pitch", R"RASGO(The improvised note in 1 V/oct, in the octave of the last learned note.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "out:surprise", R"RASGO(Rasgo deviation: how unlikely the played note was (0 = the expected one, 1 = the rarest). A CV to move the rest of the patch.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "rate", R"RASGO(Speed of the internal clock (0.05–30 Hz), when CLK is free. MARKOV plays on load, on a pentatonic walk.)RASGO"},
{"MARKOV", "temp", R"RASGO(Rasgo deviation: the temperature of the draw. 0 = always the most likely transition (repeats what it learned); 1 = the learned probabilities; 2 = nearly uniform (invents).)RASGO"},
{"MATRIX", "drift", R"RASGO(The 16 gains breathe slowly (a sum of sines, no RNG) — the matrix is never 100% static.)RASGO"},
